{"path":"io/basic_syncbuf/operator=","title":"std::basic_syncbuf<CharT,Traits,Allocator>::operator=","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::basic_syncbuf&lt;CharT,Traits,Allocator&gt;::</span>operator=","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/io/basic_syncbuf/operator=","section":"io","kind":"page","summary":"First, calls emit() to transmit all pending output (and delayed flush, if any) to the wrapped stream.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">basic_syncbuf<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> operator<span class=\"sy1\">=</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span> basic_syncbuf<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> other <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>First, calls <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_syncbuf/emit\"><code>emit()</code></a> to transmit all pending output (and delayed flush, if any) to the wrapped stream.\n</p><p>Then performs move-assignment by moving all contents from <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other</span></code>, including the temporary storage, the wrapped stream pointer, policy, and all other state (such as the mutex pointer). After move, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other</span></code> is not associated with a stream, and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other.<span class=\"me1\">get_wrapped</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> nullptr</span></code>. The put area member pointers of the base class <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_streambuf\">std::basic_streambuf</a></span> of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other</span></code> are guaranteed to be null. Destroying a moved-from <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other</span></code> will not produce any output.\n</p><p>If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/allocator_traits\"><span class=\"kw705\">std::<span class=\"me2\">allocator_traits</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Allocator<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">propagate_on_container_move_assignment</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">value</span></span></code> is <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code>, then the allocator is unchanged. Otherwise, after move-assignment, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">get_allocator<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> equals <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other.<span class=\"me1\">get_allocator</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td>  other\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td>  another std::basic_syncbuf to move from\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code>\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-notice\">This section is incomplete<br>Reason: no example </div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_osyncstream/operator=\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>operator=</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  assigns a <code>basic_osyncstream</code> object <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function of <code>std::basic_osyncstream&lt;CharT,Traits,Allocator&gt;</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div t-dsc-member-nobold-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_syncbuf/basic_syncbuf\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>(constructor)</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  constructs a <code>basic_syncbuf</code> object <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_syncbuf/emit\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>emit</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  atomically transmits the entire internal buffer to the wrapped streambuf <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_syncbuf/swap\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>swap</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  swaps two <code>basic_syncbuf</code> objects <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"io","title":"Input/output library"},{"path":"io/basic_syncbuf","title":"std::basic_syncbuf"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::basic_syncbuf<CharT,Traits,Allocator>::operator=","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. First, calls emit() to transmit all pending output (and delayed flush, if any) to the wrapped stream."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"other"},{"label":"Return value","note":"*this"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"operator=","note":"assigns a basic_osyncstream object"},{"label":"(constructor)","note":"constructs a basic_syncbuf object"},{"label":"emit","note":"atomically transmits the entire internal buffer to the wrapped streambuf"},{"label":"swap","note":"swaps two basic_syncbuf objects"}]}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":163,"codeBlockCount":0}
